// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 08-alias-validity
// facility: rule.trust.rawptr [Borrow-Exceeds-Source]; [Write-Not-Exclusive]
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.borrow-exceeds-source (static)
//
// A real soundness hole the file-based conformance suite itself found:
// neither diagnostic was ever constructed anywhere, so a function
// receiving only a `ref<T, shared>` parameter could freely mutate the
// caller's data through it by reborrowing exclusive from a shared
// source. This case exercises the reborrow path (`&mut *r`); direct
// writes (`*r = v`) and auto-deref field writes (`r.field = v`) through
// a shared reference are the same fix's other two rejected shapes,
// covered by impl/tests/conformance.rs's own regression tests for this
// facility rather than duplicated here.

fn tamper(ref<i32, shared> r) : i32
{
    auto rm = &mut *r;
    *rm = 99;
    *rm
}

fn main()
{
    i32 x = 5;
    tamper(&x);
    if (x != 99)
    {
        1 / (1 - 1);
    }
}
